Subject: lib/fnmatch.c: drop K&R-style getenv() redeclaration

Substrate's <stdlib.h> declares getenv() with the ISO C signature
(`char *getenv(const char *)`).  fnmatch.c's defensive
`extern char *getenv ();` (no args, K&R style) conflicts with the
ISO declaration under modern GCC's stricter prototype checks.

Drop the unguarded extern — every libc substrate cares about has
stdlib.h with the proper declaration, and gnulib only inserted this
defensive block for pre-ANSI systems we don't target.

---
diff -urN a/lib/fnmatch.c b/lib/fnmatch.c
--- a/lib/fnmatch.c
+++ b/lib/fnmatch.c
@@ -121,9 +121,7 @@
 /* Avoid depending on library functions or files
    whose names are inconsistent.  */

-# if !defined _LIBC && !defined getenv
-extern char *getenv ();
-# endif
+/* getenv() is declared by <stdlib.h>; the K&R-era fallback was removed. */

 # ifndef errno
 extern int errno;
